-- title:
--   From estimation to testing (Proposition 15.1)
-- statement:
--   **Proposition 15.1** (From estimation to testing). The foundational reduction underlying
--   every minimax lower bound technique in Chapter 15 (Le Cam's method, Fano's method, Assouad's
--   method): the minimax risk of estimating a functional is lower bounded by the difficulty of
--   a associated finite hypothesis-testing problem, built from any `2δ`-separated packing set of
--   the parameter space.
--
--   For any increasing $\Phi:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ and any `2δ`-separated set
--   $\{\theta_1,\dots,\theta_M\} \subseteq \theta(\mathcal P)$ with representative
--   distributions $P_{\theta_1},\dots,P_{\theta_M} \in \mathcal P$, and $Q$ the joint testing
--   measure of $(J,Z)$ built from this packing set,
--
--   $$
--   \mathfrak M\bigl(\theta(\mathcal P); \Phi\circ\rho\bigr) \;\ge\; \Phi(\delta)\, \inf_{\psi}
--   Q\bigl[\psi(Z)\ne J\bigr],
--   $$
--
--   where the infimum ranges over measurable test functions $\psi:\mathcal X \to [M]$.
--
--   This converts a continuous estimation problem into a discrete $M$-ary hypothesis testing
--   problem: every subsequent bound in the chapter (Le Cam's two-point method, Fano's method
--   via mutual information, Assouad's method) is this same reduction, specialized by a
--   particular choice of testing-error bound (Proposition 15.12 bounds `inf_ψ Q[ψ(Z)≠J]` via
--   Fano's inequality and the mutual information $I(Z;J)$).
--
--   **Formalization Note** This is the chapter's foundational lemma, not itself "Fano's
--   method" — see `description.md`'s Formalization scope for why this mission's goal was moved
--   here from the brief's originally recommended Proposition 15.12, and what remains for a
--   follow-up mission to reach the full Fano bound. `Φ` is kept fully general (not specialized
--   to `Φ(t)=t²`), and the convex-hull-free, plain packing-set hypothesis is used exactly as
--   Proposition 15.1 (not Lemma 15.9, which additionally needs convex hulls) states it.
-- source:
--   Wainwright, High-Dimensional Statistics, CUP 2019, p. 488 (PDF p. 508), Proposition 15.1, Eq. (15.3)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HighDimStat_Minimax_MinimaxRisk
import Definitions.Def_HighDimStat_Minimax_IsSeparated
import Definitions.Def_HighDimStat_Minimax_IsJointTestingMeasure

open MeasureTheory

namespace HighDimStat.Minimax

/-- **Proposition 15.1** (From estimation to testing), Wainwright, *High-Dimensional
Statistics* (2019), Eq. (15.3), p. 487. For any increasing function `Φ` and choice of
`2δ`-separated set `{θ₁,…,θ_M}` with representative distributions `P_{θⱼ}`, the minimax risk
is lower bounded as

`M(θ(P), Φ∘ρ) ≥ Φ(δ) · inf_ψ Q[ψ(Z) ≠ J]`,

where the infimum ranges over measurable test functions `ψ : 𝒳 → [M]`, and `Q` is the joint
law of `(J,Z)` generated by sampling `J` uniformly and then `Z ∼ P_{θⱼ}` given `J=j`. -/
theorem estimation_to_testing {𝒳 Ω Idx : Type*} [MeasurableSpace 𝒳] [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (measure : Idx → Measure 𝒳) [∀ p, IsProbabilityMeasure (measure p)]
    (θ : Idx → Ω) (ρ : Ω → Ω → ℝ)
    (hρ_nonneg : ∀ x y, 0 ≤ ρ x y) (hρ_refl : ∀ x, ρ x x = 0)
    (hρ_symm : ∀ x y, ρ x y = ρ y x) (hρ_tri : ∀ x y z, ρ x z ≤ ρ x y + ρ y z)
    (Φ : ℝ → ℝ) (hΦ : ∀ x y, 0 ≤ x → x ≤ y → Φ x ≤ Φ y)
    {M : ℕ} (θs : Fin M → Ω) (δ : ℝ) (hsep : IsSeparated ρ θs δ)
    (Prep : Fin M → Idx) (hPrep : ∀ j, θ (Prep j) = θs j)
    (Q : Measure (Fin M × 𝒳)) [IsProbabilityMeasure Q]
    (hQ : IsJointTestingMeasure measure Prep Q) :
    ENNReal.ofReal (Φ δ) *
      (⨅ ψ : {f : 𝒳 → Fin M // Measurable f}, Q {p : Fin M × 𝒳 | ψ.1 p.2 ≠ p.1}) ≤
      minimaxRisk measure θ ρ Φ := by sorry

end HighDimStat.Minimax
